# ADR-004: Subscription Payments

## Status: pending

## Context
Running the site on AWS incurs computing costs. Paid subscription tiers can help
sustain the site. The application needs a way to process recurring payments 
and determine which features a subscriber may use.

## Decision
Stripe will process subscription payments and manage billing. Supabase will
provide the application services used to associate Stripe customers and
subscription status with authenticated users. The subscription status will 
be used to decide access to paid features.

## Consequences
Positive: Stripe handles recurring billing and payment processing rather
  than requiring a custom payment system.
Positive: Linking subscription status to Supabase users provides an
  application identity for paid-feature access.
Negative: Subscription state must remain synchronized with Stripe, and
  access to paid features must be enforced by the application.

